//! The `bounded` reference type discipline of [TYPES-DISCIPLINE-REFERENCE]
//! (spec 0050): `// @bound n in 0..100` above a function bounds one `int`
//! parameter, every call site inside the module is checked against it by
//! interval arithmetic, and the module is erased to plain `int` for the HM
//! pipeline. The README names the subset this deliberately small checker
//! does not read.
//!
//! This directory is the checker project: the compiler builds it as one
//! program with `<compiler> <checker-directory> --compile`, one file per
//! module, and `main.ospml` is the entry. It cannot name `test`: that links
//! the TAP reporter, whose plan would follow the one response line. The suite
//! drives the built binary as a separate process and keeps its own assertions.

namespace bounded

import bounded::Checker

main () = Checker::run ()
